# Adaptation for the PinePhone Pro.
#
# Only what cannot be derived belongs here; everything else is worked out at
# runtime.

# How far below the real ambient level the ambient light sensor reads.
#
# The stk3310 sits under the cover glass next to the earpiece, and the glass
# attenuates it by one to two orders of magnitude. Measured on device, sensor
# lux against the light it was actually standing in:
#
#   palm held over the sensor      0        (dark)
#   normal room lighting           2.1-2.2  (~100-150 lux)
#   torch against the cover glass  67-123   (several thousand lux)
#
# ~50x, which is what turns those readings back into numbers the region borders
# in luna-displaymanager are expressed in. Without it every indoor reading fell
# in the DARK region, the backlight was scaled to backlightDarkScale (10%), and
# on this panel - max_brightness 51 - that is a backlight value of 4. The screen
# looked like it had failed to turn on.
#
# Not derivable: the sensor reports nothing about what is in front of it. Any
# device whose ALS is similarly covered wants its own measurement here.
deviceinfo_als_calibration="50"
